+
+## Conversation history
+
+- `validateMessage` accepts `list_conversations` independently of deployment configuration, with optional integer `limit` from 1 through 200 and optional composite `before: {updatedAt, sessionId}` whose time is a parseable string and whose id is a string; invalid fields are refused with an error naming the field ([validated by: accepts history requests and composite cursors, rejecting invalid fields by name](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L75)).
+- History is separately opt-in through `transport.history.enabled`, default off; a disabled deployment or a store without `listFor` answers a history request with exactly one `error` carrying `UNSUPPORTED`, never an empty list or a `stream_end` ([validated by: refuses history with UNSUPPORTED when disabled or the store has no listFor](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L146)).
+- A history request is answered outside the per-session turn lock, before a pending turn's `stream_end`, and no `conversation_list` is pushed unsolicited ([validated by: answers a history request before the pending turn ends and never pushes a list unsolicited](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L170)).
+
+- A store failure answers exactly one sanitized `SERVER_ERROR` and is logged with the session id without user content, while a collection adapter without `find` answers `UNSUPPORTED`; both leave the socket open for subsequent requests ([validated by: sanitizes store failures, distinguishes an adapter without find, and keeps the socket usable](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L216)).
